he solver’s own artificial arcs are unbounded).","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero; capacities, supplies and costs fit in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Σ capacity × |cost| fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (checked before solving; it bounds the total","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cost, so a cost that could not be represented traps here rather than wrapping);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the solver’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs; computed in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never reported); the positive supplies sum within ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A least-cost flow meeting every supply (positive: the vertex sends that much more than it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives; negative: a demand), within capacities (LEMON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkSimplex"},{"type":"text","text":", OR-Tools"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SimpleMinCostFlow"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min_cost_flow"},{"type":"text","text":" with the opposite sign), or nil when there is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none: the supplies do not sum to zero, or some set of vertices supplies more than its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out-edges carry. Costs may be negative; negative cycles are saturated (capacities are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finite). A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees, LEMON’s layout."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supply"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, then, for each edge in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cost"},{"type":"text","text":", before any work. Which optimum is returned when several"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exist is unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result."}],"references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumcostflow(supply:capacity:cost:)","type":"topic","title":"minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","abstract":[{"text":"A least-cost flow meeting every supply (positive: the vertex sends that much more than it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives; negative: a demand), within capacities (LEMON ","type":"text"},{"code":"NetworkSimplex","type":"codeV